# Secrets manifest — the data behind `bin/secrets`.
#
# Each record describes one environment variable that has to be pasted in by
# hand on a new machine. Adding a secret means adding a record here; the wizard
# itself never needs editing.
#
#   name:     the exported variable name
#   scope:    core (every machine) | carwow (work machines only)
#   label:    one-line description, shown as the prompt
#   url:      where to go to mint the token
#   pattern:  optional ERE the value is checked against (a mismatch warns,
#             it does not block — token formats change)
#   help:     repeatable; one instruction line each
#
# Records are separated by a line containing only `---`.

name: GITHUB_TOKEN
scope: core
label: GitHub personal access token
url: https://github.com/settings/tokens
pattern: ^(ghp_|gho_|ghs_|github_pat_)[A-Za-z0-9_]{20,}$
help: Choose "Generate new token (classic)".
help: Scopes: repo, read:org, gist, workflow.
help: Set a 90-day expiry and copy the value before leaving the page —
help: GitHub shows it exactly once.

---

name: GITHUB_PACKAGES_TOKEN
scope: carwow
label: GitHub token for the carwow private package registry
url: https://github.com/settings/tokens
pattern: ^(ghp_|gho_|ghs_|github_pat_)[A-Za-z0-9_]{20,}$
help: A second classic token, kept separate from GITHUB_TOKEN so it can be
help: scoped down to package reads only.
help: Scopes: read:packages, repo.
help: Used by bundler and npm to pull carwow's private gems and packages.

---

name: HONEYCOMB_CLAUDE_TELEMETRY_KEY
scope: carwow
label: Honeycomb ingest key for Claude Code telemetry
url: https://ui.honeycomb.io/carwow/environments/ai-tooling/api_keys
pattern: ^[A-Za-z0-9_]{20,}$
help: This is an *ingest* key (write-only), not a management key.
help: Create one with "Can send events" and nothing else.
help: It ends up in OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS, sending Claude Code traces
help: to the "claude-code" dataset. Leave blank to turn telemetry off.

---

name: HONEYCOMB_TOKEN
scope: carwow
label: Honeycomb management key for the query API
url: https://ui.honeycomb.io/carwow/environments/$legacy$/api_keys
pattern: ^[A-Za-z0-9_]{20,}$
help: A *management* / configuration key — this one can read data back, so
help: it is the more sensitive of the two Honeycomb keys.
help: Needs "Manage queries and columns" plus "Run queries".
help: Used by the sre:honeycomb skill to query production telemetry.

---

name: BUGSNAG_AUTH_TOKEN
scope: carwow
label: Bugsnag personal auth token
url: https://app.bugsnag.com/settings/carwow/my-account/auth-tokens
pattern: ^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$
help: Generate one under "Personal auth tokens".
help: It is a UUID, and it inherits your full account access — treat it as a
help: password and rotate it if it is ever pasted anywhere shared.
help: Used by the Bugsnag MCP server.
